From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display/msm: dpu: add the optional LUTDMA register set

The DPU's LUTDMA engine loads the DSPP and SSPP LUT blocks over the LUT
bus from a command buffer. It sits in the MDSS register space outside
the "mdp" range, so let the DPU node name it as a third, optional reg
entry "lutdma".

---
diff -ruN a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sc7280-dpu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sc7280-dpu.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sc7280-dpu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sc7280-dpu.yaml
@@ -25,14 +25,18 @@
       - qcom,sm8550-dpu
 
   reg:
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - description: Address offset and size for mdp register set
       - description: Address offset and size for vbif register set
+      - description: Address offset and size for the LUTDMA engine register set
 
   reg-names:
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - const: mdp
       - const: vbif
+      - const: lutdma
 
   clocks:
     items:
diff -ruN a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8650-dpu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8650-dpu.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8650-dpu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/qcom,sm8650-dpu.yaml
@@ -29,14 +29,18 @@
           - const: qcom,sa8775p-dpu
 
   reg:
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - description: Address offset and size for mdp register set
       - description: Address offset and size for vbif register set
+      - description: Address offset and size for the LUTDMA engine register set
 
   reg-names:
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - const: mdp
       - const: vbif
+      - const: lutdma
 
   clocks:
     items:
